    <p class="bhd-page__kicker">RUN THE RIVER FALL CHALLENGE</p>
    <h2>Train for the distance you are actually running</h2>
    <p>Run the River Fall Challenge is scheduled for September 27 in Edmonton with 5K, 10K and half-marathon distances. A 5K and a half marathon do not create the same hydration problem, so your plan should follow the distance, pace, weather and what you already know you tolerate.</p>
    <p>For longer sessions, warmer conditions or heavier sweating, a prepared electrolyte drink can be useful. For shorter or easier work, ordinary water and meals may be enough.</p>
  </div>
